    "content": "Mogadishu — The Speaker of Somalia's federal parliament, Abdulkadir Mohamed Nur Jama, has directed the parliamentary secretariat to compile a list of lawmakers who regularly miss assembly sessions, with the aim of suspending their salaries and stipends by September. According to reporting by Somali Stream, approximately 50 members of parliament could be affected if the measure is implemented. This would mark the first time a sitting speaker has taken such a step against absenteeism in the legislature.\n\nThe move comes shortly after Jama assumed the speaker's office, signaling an early focus on parliamentary discipline. Absenteeism has long been a concern in Somalia's parliament, where sessions often struggle to reach quorum, delaying votes on key legislation. The speaker's directive tasks the secretariat with identifying repeat absentees, after which their pay would be withheld starting in September.\n\nSomalia's parliament has faced repeated criticism for low attendance and slow legislative progress. Lawmakers are expected to attend sessions regularly, but enforcement mechanisms have been weak. Jama's initiative, if carried out, would establish a precedent for holding members accountable for their attendance. The exact criteria for determining frequent absence have not been publicly detailed.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, which closely follows political developments in the homeland and often funds or advocates for legislative priorities, the move could be seen as a step toward greater accountability. Many in the diaspora have expressed frustration over perceived inefficiency in the federal parliament, and any effort to improve attendance may resonate with those who remit money or engage in political advocacy. However, the practical impact will depend on how rigorously the policy is enforced.\n\nThe speaker's directive is part of a broader effort to strengthen parliamentary operations. It remains to be seen whether the measure will face resistance from lawmakers or be fully implemented. The parliament secretariat has not announced a timeline for releasing the list of absentees.\n\nRead the original report from Somalia Guardian here: https://www.somaliguardian.com/news/somalia-news/somalia-parliament-speaker-cut-pay-absent-lawmakers/",
    "source": "somaliguardian.com",
